    "Full long-history configuration retained under unchanged compact-context bound; original evaluator catalogs and frozen transport sources preserved."
  ],
  "known_limits": [
    "No physical execution of this changed compact owner contract; original twenty-method run belongs to frozen HTTPv3.",
    "Current product bindings remain M1-only; final-M4 profiles exist separately and are not relabeled observations.",
    "Emergency channel is owned by the current process; no crash/restart cleanup recovery claim.",
    "Unresolved normal removal is never retried or promoted by cleanup; earlier main observation failure remains.",
    "Boundary scans still grow with history. No whole-executor speedup is inferred from the previous storage-only replay.",
    "Retention-triggered socket teardown assumes ordinary socket behavior; repeated asynchronous interruption and OS close failure are not qualified.",
    "Incremental type coverage retains117 known legacy diagnostics and is not whole-repository type safety."
